VERDICT: UNMEASURED -- the action cannot be armed on this bench's config.
===========================================================================
      IE520-stk(config-if)# loop-protection action port-disable
      % Port-disable action is not supported with fast blocking

The bench baseline carries `loop-protection loop-detect ldf-interval 1
fast-block`, and port-disable is mutually exclusive with fast-block. Clearing
fast-block was attempted and did NOT work:
  - `no loop-protection loop-detect fast-block`  -> % Invalid input
  - `no loop-protection ?` offers only `loop-detect` and <cr>, i.e. it
    disables loop detection wholesale rather than just the fast-block flag
  - re-issuing `loop-protection loop-detect ldf-interval 1` WITHOUT the
    fast-block keyword does not clear it -- `show loop-protection` still
    reports `Fast Block: Enabled`
So on this build fast-block appears to be sticky once set, and the only way
found to remove it would be `no loop-protection loop-detect` (turning loop
detection off entirely), which defeats the case.

RECORDED AS A DECISION for review: is fast-block meant to be clearable without
disabling loop-detect? If so, the missing negation is the finding. If not, the
case needs a precondition saying fast-block must never have been enabled.

Confirmed working syntax for the record:
  interface <port> / loop-protection action {learn-disable | link-down |
  log-only | none | port-disable | vlan-disable}
  (NOT `loop-protection loop-detect action ...`, which is unrecognised)
Also: loop-protection cannot be configured on an aggregator MEMBER port --
`% port4.0.2: Loop detection can not be configured on aggregator member ports`.
